The souvenirs change its internal operators.

An invariant changes what it preserves.

A new distinction changes what it can perceive.

A failed route changes its priors.

A new category changes what it can represent.

A transform changes what it can do.

A junction changes where it can travel.

A question changes what it searches for.

A new sense changes what world is addressable.

So:

\boxed{\text{Souvenir}=\text{anything that changes future reachable behavior}}

is one possible after-the-fact definition—but importantly, we don’t give that definition to the outgoing imps.

Let them decide.

Then Decrypto what their choices reveal about souvenirness itself.

That’s the experiment.

